IMPORT prelude

-- First Home Owner Grant and Other Home Owner Grants Act 2000 (Qld), read with the First Home Owner Grant and Other
-- Home Owner Grants Regulation 2021 (Qld).
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules are written in the Act's own actors and terms: "the applicant", "the applicant's
-- spouse", "the commissioner", "an interested person". The first home buyer's questions are in fhog-seat.l4, which
-- IMPORTs this module and restates no rule.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. Part 2 Division 2: s 4 (eligibility criteria), s 5 (eligible transaction, with the $750,000 caps
-- in s 5(6) to (9) and the s 5(4), (5) scheme presumption as facts), s 6 (home, new home), s 7 (home owner), s 8 with
-- Regulation r 2 (relevant interest), s 8A (unencumbered value, as a stated value), s 9 (spouse). Part 3: s 10 (when the
-- grant is payable), ss 11 to 15 (criteria 1 to 5), s 16 (application period), s 17 with Regulation r 3 (interested
-- persons), s 20 (amount), ss 25EA, 25EB (relevant eligible transactions, 20 November 2023 to 30 June 2026), s 22
-- (payment in anticipation of the residence requirements), s 22A (repayment after completion over the cap), s 23
-- (conditions). Part 4 Division 3: s 47 (repayment and penalty), s 48 (debt, joint and several, instalments) with
-- Regulation r 4 (interest), s 49 (charge over the land). Regulation r 6 (the prescribed completion requirement).
-- Part 5: ss 56 to 59 (objection within 60 days, review by QCAT).
--
-- WHICH VERSION GOVERNS. The deposit is the Act in force from 1 July 2026. Section 91 says that for an eligible
-- transaction whose commencement date is before 1 July 2026 the Act "continues to apply ... as if this Act had not
-- been amended by the Revenue (Cost of Living Relief Locked-in Law) and Other Legislation Amendment Act 2026, part 3".
-- That earlier version is not deposited. READING: Part 3 Division 7 (ss 25EA, 25EB), which covers only contracts made
-- and building begun between 20 November 2023 and 30 June 2026, is applied as it stands in the deposit, and so are
-- ss 5 to 17 for those transactions. An amount that would come from s 20 as it stood before 1 July 2026, or from an
-- even older version (ss 79 to 81 for 2012, Divisions 5 and 6), answers `not covered`. See NOTES.md, findings 1 and 2.
--
-- Edition: act-2000-014, the version in force from 2026-07-01, as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2000-014.txt (retrieved 2026-10-20); sl-2021-0018, the version in force from
-- 2021-03-19, as deposited at
-- ../../../first-home-owner-grant-and-other-home-owner-grants-regulation-2021/registers/source-bundle/sl-2021-0018.txt.
-- Based on content from the Queensland Legislation website at 20 October 2026 (CC BY 4.0, the State of Queensland).
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `First Home Owner Grant and Other Home Owner Grants Act 2000 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `Dates the Act uses, and counting`

`1 July 2000`      MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2000
`11 October 2012`  MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 11 10 2012
`20 November 2023` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 20 11 2023
`30 June 2026`     MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 2026
`1 July 2026`      MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 1 7 2026

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the other day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`on or before` `the day` `the other day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day` AT MOST DATE_SERIAL `the other day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `the other day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`strictly before` `the day` `the other day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the other day`

GIVEN `the earlier day` IS A DATE
      `the later day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the earlier day` `to` `the later day` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the later day` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the earlier day`

GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`add days to` `the day` `n` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS `n`)

GIVEN `m` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days in month` `m` `of` `y` MEANS
    IF `m` EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (`m` PLUS 1) `y`) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 `m` `y`)

-- A period of months from a day ends on the same day of the later month, or on that month's last day where it is
-- shorter (31 August plus 6 months is 28 or 29 February). READING: the Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), which counts
-- periods, is not deposited; this is the usual reckoning, with the day the period starts from left out.
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
      `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`add months to` `the day` `n` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the day`) (`the days in month` `the month` `of` `the year`)) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS `n`
        `the year`        MEANS TRUNC (`the month count` DIVIDED BY 12) 0
        `the month`       MEANS (`the month count` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

-- "1 year after" a day: the same day of the next year (29 February: 28 February).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`1 year after` `the day` MEANS `add months to` `the day` 12

§§ `s 6 -- home and new home`

-- s 6(1): "A home is a building, fixed to land, that-- (a) may lawfully be used as a place of residence; and (b) is a
-- suitable building for use as a place of residence."
-- s 6(2): "A new home is a home that-- (a) has not been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence; or (b) is
-- a substantially renovated home."
-- s 6(3): substantially renovated if "(a) the home is the subject of a contract for the purchase of the home; and (b) the
-- sale ... is, under the A New Tax System (Goods and Services Tax) Act 1999 (Cwlth), a taxable supply as a sale of new
-- residential premises as defined under section 40-75(1)(b) of that Act; and (c) the home, as renovated, has not been
-- previously occupied or sold as a place of residence." Whether the sale is such a taxable supply is a borrowed
-- (Commonwealth) term: a fact. For a home still to be built, the facts are those of the home as it will be built.
DECLARE `Home facts` HAS
    `is a building fixed to land`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `may lawfully be used as a place of residence`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a suitable building for use as a place of residence`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the subject of a contract for its purchase`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `as renovated, has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a home (s 6(1))` IF
        `the home`'s `is a building fixed to land`
    AND `the home`'s `may lawfully be used as a place of residence`
    AND `the home`'s `is a suitable building for use as a place of residence`

GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a substantially renovated home (s 6(3))` IF
        `the home`'s `is the subject of a contract for its purchase`
    AND `the home`'s `its sale is a taxable supply of new residential premises under GST Act s 40-75(1)(b)`
    AND (NOT (`the home`'s `as renovated, has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`))

GIVEN `the home` IS A `Home facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a new home (s 6(2))` IF
        `it is a home (s 6(1))` `the home`
    AND (   (NOT (`the home`'s `has been previously occupied or sold as a place of residence`))
         OR `it is a substantially renovated home (s 6(3))` `the home`)

§§ `s 8 and Regulation r 2 -- relevant interest; s 7 -- home owner`

-- s 8(1): a relevant interest in land is (a) an estate in fee simple; (b) a life estate; (c) a perpetual lease granted
-- by the Commonwealth or the State; (d) a leasehold interest granted by the Commonwealth or the State "that may be
-- converted into an estate in fee simple"; (e) "a term lease for pastoral purposes granted under the Land Act 1994";
-- (f) an interest as purchaser of the fee simple by instalments, from the Commonwealth or the State or an
-- instrumentality, or under "an instalment contract under the Property Law Act 2023, section 89"; (g) a licence or right
-- of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the State "that gives, in the commissioner's opinion, ... reasonable
-- security of tenure"; (h) an interest in a company's shares "if the commissioner is satisfied" that it gives exclusive
-- occupation of a specified home owned by the company, built before the interest was acquired, the shares being worth
-- not less than the company's interest in the home; (i) "another interest declared by regulation".
-- Regulation r 2(1) declares: (a) and (b) a right, given by a relative, to occupy a detached dwelling built or to be
-- built (under the person's contract, or by an owner builder) on part of land the relative owns; (c) a right to occupy
-- a mobile home under a relevant agreement; (d) a manufactured home owner's interest in a site agreement; (e) "a
-- sublessee's interest under a lease mentioned in section 8(1)(d) of the Act that is for a term of at least 10 years";
-- (f) an interest in a lease under the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 s 120(2)(a) or the Torres Strait Islander Land Act 1991
-- s 85(2)(a). r 2(3): "relative" is a parent, grandparent, child, stepchild, brother or sister of the person or the
-- person's spouse, or the spouse of any of them.
DECLARE `Kind of interest` IS ONE OF
    `an estate in fee simple`
    `a life estate`
    `a perpetual lease granted by the Commonwealth or the State`
    `a lease granted by the Commonwealth or the State that may be converted into fee simple`
    `a term lease for pastoral purposes under the Land Act 1994`
    `an interest as purchaser of the fee simple by instalments`
    `a licence or right of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the State`
    `an interest in company shares giving exclusive occupation of a home the company owns`
    `a right given by a relative to occupy a detached dwelling on part of the relative's land`
    `a right to occupy a mobile home under a relevant agreement`
    `a manufactured home owner's interest in a site agreement`
    `a sublessee's interest under a convertible lease for a term of at least 10 years`
    `an interest in a lease under the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 or the Torres Strait Islander Land Act 1991`
    `another interest`

-- s 8(2): "(a) an interest is not a relevant interest at a particular time unless the holder of the interest has, or
-- will have within 1 year after that time, a right to immediate occupation of the land; and (b) an interest is not a
-- relevant interest in the hands of a person who holds it subject to a trust." s 8(4): where a guardian holds it on
-- trust for "a person under a legal disability", that person "is taken to be the person who holds a relevant interest".
DECLARE `Interest facts` HAS
    `the kind of interest`                                                     IS A `Kind of interest`
    `the commissioner considers the licence or right gives reasonable security of tenure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied of the share conditions in s 8(1)(h)`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder has, or will have within 1 year, a right to immediate occupation of the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person holds it subject to a trust`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `a guardian holds it on trust for the person, who is under a legal disability` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `its kind is listed in s 8(1) or Regulation r 2(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the interest`'s `the kind of interest`
    WHEN `a licence or right of occupancy granted by the Commonwealth or the State` THEN
        `the interest`'s `the commissioner considers the licence or right gives reasonable security of tenure`
    WHEN `an interest in company shares giving exclusive occupation of a home the company owns` THEN
        `the interest`'s `the commissioner is satisfied of the share conditions in s 8(1)(h)`
    WHEN `another interest` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the interest` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the interest is a relevant interest of the person (s 8)` IF
        `its kind is listed in s 8(1) or Regulation r 2(1)` `the interest`
    AND `the interest`'s `the holder has, or will have within 1 year, a right to immediate occupation of the land`
    AND (   `the interest`'s `a guardian holds it on trust for the person, who is under a legal disability`
         OR (NOT (`the interest`'s `the person holds it subject to a trust`)))

-- Regulation r 2(1): the declared interests. r 3(1)(a) turns on whether the applicant's interest is one of them.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `Kind of interest`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an interest declared by Regulation r 2(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a right given by a relative to occupy a detached dwelling on part of the relative's land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a right to occupy a mobile home under a relevant agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a manufactured home owner's interest in a site agreement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a sublessee's interest under a convertible lease for a term of at least 10 years` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an interest in a lease under the Aboriginal Land Act 1991 or the Torres Strait Islander Land Act 1991` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 7: "A person is a home owner or owner of a home if the person has a relevant interest in the land on which the home
-- is built." The schedule: owner, for land, is "a person who has a relevant interest in the land".
GIVEN `the interest` IS AN `Interest facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an owner of the home (s 7)` IF `the interest is a relevant interest of the person (s 8)` `the interest`

§§ `s 8A -- unencumbered value`

-- s 8A(1): the unencumbered value of a home, land or relevant interest in land "is the value of the property determined
-- without regard to-- (a) any encumbrance ...; or (b) any arrangement-- (i) the parties to which are not dealing with
-- each other at arm's length; and (ii) that results in the reduction of the value of the property; or (c) any
-- arrangement for which a significant purpose of any party ... was, in the commissioner's opinion, the reduction of the
-- value". It is a valuation rule, not a computation: the encoding takes the value as stated on that basis (s 69B lets
-- the commissioner require or obtain a valuation; out of scope).

§§ `s 9 -- spouse`

-- s 9(1): a spouse is a person who is married, a de facto partner, or a civil partner. (2): "A person is a de facto
-- partner of another person only if they are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis ... and, for at
-- least 2 years, have so lived together as a couple." (3), (4): a married or civil partner "living apart" with "no
-- intention of again living together as a couple", if the commissioner is satisfied of that, "must not be regarded as
-- the applicant's spouse". (5), (6): a de facto partner living apart who, the commissioner is satisfied, intends "to
-- again live together as a couple" "must be regarded as the applicant's spouse".
DECLARE `Relationship` IS ONE OF
    `married`
    `in a civil partnership`
    `living together as a couple without being married or in a civil partnership`
    `no partner`

DECLARE `Partner facts` HAS
    `the relationship`                                                         IS A `Relationship`
    `they are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the years they have lived together as a couple`                           IS A NUMBER
    `they are living apart`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied they have no intention of again living together as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied they intend to again live together as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the partner` IS A `Partner facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the partner is the applicant's spouse (s 9)` IF
    CONSIDER `the partner`'s `the relationship`
    WHEN `married` THEN `not excluded by s 9(3), (4)`
    WHEN `in a civil partnership` THEN `not excluded by s 9(3), (4)`
    WHEN `living together as a couple without being married or in a civil partnership` THEN
            `the partner`'s `the years they have lived together as a couple` AT LEAST 2
        AND (   `the partner`'s `they are living together as a couple on a genuine domestic basis`
             OR (    `the partner`'s `they are living apart`
                 AND `the partner`'s `the commissioner is satisfied they intend to again live together as a couple`))
    WHEN `no partner` THEN FALSE
    WHERE
        `not excluded by s 9(3), (4)` MEANS
            (NOT (    `the partner`'s `they are living apart`
                  AND `the partner`'s `the commissioner is satisfied they have no intention of again living together as a couple`))

§§ `ss 11 to 14 -- eligibility criteria 1 to 4`

-- s 12(1): "an Australian citizen or a permanent resident". Schedule: "permanent resident means-- (a) the holder of a
-- permanent visa as defined by the Migration Act 1958 (Cwlth), section 30(1); or (b) a New Zealand citizen who is the
-- holder of a special category visa as defined by the Migration Act 1958 (Cwlth), section 32." Borrowed terms: facts.
DECLARE `Citizenship or residence` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `the holder of a permanent visa`
    `a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa`
    `none of these`

-- s 13(1): ineligible if "(a) the applicant or the applicant's spouse has been a party to an earlier application under
-- this Act or a corresponding law; and (b) a grant was paid on the application." (2): not ineligible if "(a) the grant
-- was later paid back; and (b) the basis for the repayment ... was a failure to satisfy section 10(1); and (c) any
-- penalty amount payable under section 47 was also paid".
DECLARE `Earlier grant facts` HAS
    `was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `that grant was paid back because s 10(1) was not satisfied, with any s 47 penalty` IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 14(1): ineligible if the applicant or spouse "has, before 1 July 2000, held-- (a) a relevant interest in
-- residential property in Queensland; or (b) an interest in residential property in another State that is a relevant
-- interest under a corresponding law of that State." (2): not if the interest was as purchaser under a s 8(1)(f)
-- contract "terminated within 1 year after the contract was entered into" and the fee simple was not acquired.
-- (4): ineligible if the applicant or spouse "has, on or after 1 July 2000 and before the date on which the application
-- is made, held an interest in property (other than the property to which the application relates) used at any time on
-- or after 1 July 2000 as the residence of the applicant or the applicant's spouse", being such an interest. (5): the
-- property is "taken not to have" been so used if it "was the subject of an earlier application under this Act by the
-- applicant", a grant was paid, and the applicant repaid it "because of a failure to satisfy criterion 5". (3): a
-- deferred right of occupation because the property was leased is disregarded. Schedule: "residential property means
-- land in Australia that, at a particular time, has a building on it that is lawfully occupied as a place of residence
-- or is suitable for occupation as a place of residence." Whether an interest in another State is a relevant interest
-- under that State's corresponding law is a borrowed term: a fact.
DECLARE `Earlier property facts` HAS
    `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `that interest was as purchaser by instalments, the contract ended within 1 year and the fee simple was not acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `held, from 1 July 2000 and before the application, a relevant interest in other residential property used as the residence of the applicant or spouse` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that property was the subject of the applicant's earlier application whose grant was repaid for failing criterion 5` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Applicant facts` HAS
    `is a natural person`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `age at the commencement date`                                             IS A NUMBER
    `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from the age requirement (s 11(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `citizenship or residence`                                                 IS A `Citizenship or residence`
    `another joint applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `own earlier grant`                                                        IS AN `Earlier grant facts`
    `own earlier property`                                                     IS AN `Earlier property facts`
    `partner`                                                                  IS A `Partner facts`
    `partner's earlier grant`                                                  IS AN `Earlier grant facts`
    `partner's earlier property`                                               IS AN `Earlier property facts`

-- s 11(1): "(a) a natural person; and (b) at least 18 years of age at the commencement date for the eligible
-- transaction." (2): the commissioner may exempt from (1)(b) if satisfied the applicant will comply with criterion 5
-- and the application is not part of a scheme. The exemption is the commissioner's: a fact.
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant meets criterion 1 (s 11)` IF
        `the applicant`'s `is a natural person`
    AND (   `the applicant`'s `age at the commencement date` AT LEAST 18
         OR `the applicant`'s `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from the age requirement (s 11(2))`)

GIVEN `the status` IS A `Citizenship or residence`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` IF
    CONSIDER `the status`
    WHEN `none of these` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 12(2): "If an application is made by joint applicants and 1 of the applicants is an Australian citizen or a
-- permanent resident, it is not necessary for the other or others to be".
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant meets criterion 2 (s 12)` IF
        `is an Australian citizen or permanent resident` (`the applicant`'s `citizenship or residence`)
    OR  `the applicant`'s `another joint applicant is an Australian citizen or permanent resident`

GIVEN `the history` IS AN `Earlier grant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier grant counts (s 13)` IF
        `the history`'s `was a party to an earlier application on which a grant was paid`
    AND (NOT (`the history`'s `that grant was paid back because s 10(1) was not satisfied, with any s 47 penalty`))

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant meets criterion 3 (s 13)` IF
    (NOT (   `an earlier grant counts (s 13)` (`the applicant`'s `own earlier grant`)
          OR (    `the partner is the applicant's spouse (s 9)` (`the applicant`'s `partner`)
              AND `an earlier grant counts (s 13)` (`the applicant`'s `partner's earlier grant`))))

GIVEN `the history` IS AN `Earlier property facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an earlier property interest counts (s 14)` IF
        (    `the history`'s `held a relevant interest in residential property before 1 July 2000`
         AND (NOT (`the history`'s `that interest was as purchaser by instalments, the contract ended within 1 year and the fee simple was not acquired`)))
    OR  (    `the history`'s `held, from 1 July 2000 and before the application, a relevant interest in other residential property used as the residence of the applicant or spouse`
         AND (NOT (`the history`'s `that property was the subject of the applicant's earlier application whose grant was repaid for failing criterion 5`)))

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant meets criterion 4 (s 14)` IF
    (NOT (   `an earlier property interest counts (s 14)` (`the applicant`'s `own earlier property`)
          OR (    `the partner is the applicant's spouse (s 9)` (`the applicant`'s `partner`)
              AND `an earlier property interest counts (s 14)` (`the applicant`'s `partner's earlier property`))))

DECLARE `Criteria answer` IS ONE OF
    `meets criteria 1 to 4`
    `fails criterion 1: not a natural person (s 11(1)(a))`
    `fails criterion 1: under 18 at the commencement date and not exempted (s 11(1)(b), (2))`
    `fails criterion 2: not an Australian citizen or permanent resident, and no joint applicant is (s 12)`
    `fails criterion 3: the applicant or the applicant's spouse has received an earlier grant (s 13)`
    `fails criterion 4: the applicant or the applicant's spouse has held a relevant interest in residential property (s 14)`

-- The first criterion failed, in the Act's order.
GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN `Applicant facts`
GIVETH A `Criteria answer`
`the criteria 1 to 4 answer for` `the applicant` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the applicant`'s `is a natural person`))
    THEN `fails criterion 1: not a natural person (s 11(1)(a))`
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the applicant meets criterion 1 (s 11)` `the applicant`))
         THEN `fails criterion 1: under 18 at the commencement date and not exempted (s 11(1)(b), (2))`
         ELSE IF (NOT (`the applicant meets criterion 2 (s 12)` `the applicant`))
              THEN `fails criterion 2: not an Australian citizen or permanent resident, and no joint applicant is (s 12)`
              ELSE IF (NOT (`the applicant meets criterion 3 (s 13)` `the applicant`))
                   THEN `fails criterion 3: the applicant or the applicant's spouse has received an earlier grant (s 13)`
                   ELSE IF (NOT (`the applicant meets criterion 4 (s 14)` `the applicant`))
                        THEN `fails criterion 4: the applicant or the applicant's spouse has held a relevant interest in residential property (s 14)`
                        ELSE `meets criteria 1 to 4`

§§ `s 15 -- criterion 5, the residence requirements`

-- s 15(1): the applicant "must occupy the home ... as the applicant's principal place of residence for a continuous
-- period of at least 6 months." (2): if satisfied "there are good reasons to do so", the commissioner may "(a) approve a
-- shorter period; or (b) exempt the applicant from the requirement to comply with subsection (1)." (3): the period
-- "must start within 1 year after completion of the eligible transaction or a longer period approved by the
-- commissioner." (4): the commissioner may exempt "from the residence requirement under subsection (3)" a joint
-- applicant if "at least 1 of the applicants complies with the residence requirement" and there are good reasons.
-- (5): approvals and exemptions may be given at any time, even after the period has ended.
-- READING: s 15(4) lifts only the subsection (3) requirement, the start within 1 year; a full exemption is under
-- s 15(2)(b). See NOTES.md, finding 9. Every approval and exemption is the commissioner's: a fact.
DECLARE `Residence facts` HAS
    `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from s 15(1) (s 15(2)(b))`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner has approved a shorter period (s 15(2)(a))`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the approved shorter period, in months`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `the commissioner has approved a longer period to start (s 15(3))`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of the approved longer period to start`                      IS A DATE
    `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from s 15(3) as a joint applicant (s 15(4))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `another joint applicant complies with the residence requirement`         IS A BOOLEAN

`the residence period in months (s 15(1))` MEANS 6

GIVEN `the residence` IS A `Residence facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the months the applicant must occupy the home` `the residence` MEANS
    IF `the residence`'s `the commissioner has approved a shorter period (s 15(2)(a))`
    THEN `the residence`'s `the approved shorter period, in months`
    ELSE `the residence period in months (s 15(1))`

GIVEN `the residence` IS A `Residence facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the start deadline applies to the applicant` IF
    (NOT (    `the residence`'s `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from s 15(3) as a joint applicant (s 15(4))`
          AND `the residence`'s `another joint applicant complies with the residence requirement`))

GIVEN `the residence` IS A `Residence facts`
      `the completion date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to start occupying the home` `the residence` `the completion date` MEANS
    IF `the residence`'s `the commissioner has approved a longer period to start (s 15(3))`
    THEN `the residence`'s `the last day of the approved longer period to start`
    ELSE `1 year after` `the completion date`

-- The day the required period ends: the applicant must still occupy the home on every day before it.
GIVEN `the residence` IS A `Residence facts`
      `the day occupation started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day the required period ends` `the residence` `the day occupation started` MEANS
    `add months to` `the day occupation started` (`the months the applicant must occupy the home` `the residence`)

-- Where the applicant is in occupation on the day asked: the continuous period relied on, its first day, and whether
-- (and when) it ended.
DECLARE `Occupation facts` HAS
    `has started to occupy the home as principal place of residence`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first day of the continuous period of occupation`                     IS A DATE
    `that period of occupation has ended`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the first day the home was no longer the principal place of residence`   IS A DATE

DECLARE `Residence answer` IS ONE OF
    `exempt from the residence requirements (s 15(2)(b))`
    `the residence requirements are complied with`
    `not yet complied with, and there is still time`
    `not complied with: occupation did not start in time (s 15(3))`
    `not complied with: occupation ended before the required period (s 15(1))`

-- Schedule, "residence requirements": the s 15(1) occupation (or the shorter period) and the s 15(3) start.
GIVEN `the residence`       IS A `Residence facts`
      `the occupation`      IS AN `Occupation facts`
      `the completion date` IS A DATE
      `the day asked`       IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Residence answer`
`the residence answer` `the residence` `the occupation` `the completion date` `the day asked` MEANS
    IF `the residence`'s `the commissioner has exempted the applicant from s 15(1) (s 15(2)(b))`
    THEN `exempt from the residence requirements (s 15(2)(b))`
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the occupation`'s `has started to occupy the home as principal place of residence`))
         THEN IF     `the start deadline applies to the applicant` `the residence`
                 AND `strictly before` (`the last day to start occupying the home` `the residence` `the completion date`) `the day asked`
              THEN `not complied with: occupation did not start in time (s 15(3))`
              ELSE `not yet complied with, and there is still time`
         ELSE IF     `the start deadline applies to the applicant` `the residence`
                 AND `strictly before` (`the last day to start occupying the home` `the residence` `the completion date`) (`the occupation`'s `the first day of the continuous period of occupation`)
              THEN `not complied with: occupation did not start in time (s 15(3))`
              ELSE IF `the occupation`'s `that period of occupation has ended`
                   THEN IF `strictly before` (`the occupation`'s `the first day the home was no longer the principal place of residence`) `the end of the period`
                        THEN `not complied with: occupation ended before the required period (s 15(1))`
                        ELSE `the residence requirements are complied with`
                   ELSE IF `on or before` `the end of the period` `the day asked`
                        THEN `the residence requirements are complied with`
                        ELSE `not yet complied with, and there is still time`
    WHERE
        `the end of the period` MEANS
            `the day the required period ends` `the residence` (`the occupation`'s `the first day of the continuous period of occupation`)

§§ `s 5 -- eligible transaction, and the $750,000 caps`

-- s 5(1): "(a) a contract made on or after 1 July 2000 for the purchase of a new home in the State; or (b) a
-- comprehensive home building contract made by the owner of land in the State, or a person who will on completion of
-- the contract be the owner of land in the State, to have a new home built on the land ...; or (c) the building of a
-- new home in the State by an owner builder if the building work starts on or after 1 July 2000." (2): the same for a
-- home "other than a new home", if made or started "before 11 October 2012". (3): a contract is one for the purchase
-- of a home if it is for "the acquisition of a relevant interest in land-- (a) on which a new home or other home is
-- built; or (b) on which a new home or other home is to be built, before completion of the contract, by or for the
-- vendor and at the expense of the vendor."
DECLARE `Kind of transaction` IS ONE OF
    `a contract to buy a home`
    `a comprehensive home building contract`
    `building a home as an owner builder`

-- s 5(4): a contract "is not an eligible transaction if the commissioner is satisfied it forms part of a scheme to
-- circumvent limitations on, or requirements affecting, eligibility or entitlement". (5): "Unless satisfied to the
-- contrary, the commissioner must presume" such a scheme if an option or right to the contract was granted before
-- 1 July 2000. s 25EA(2), (3): the same for a relevant eligible transaction, presumed where the contract replaces one
-- made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a substantially similar home, or an option or right was granted before
-- that date. The commissioner's satisfaction is a fact.
DECLARE `Transaction facts` HAS
    `kind`                                                                     IS A `Kind of transaction`
    `the home is in Queensland`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the home`                                                                 IS A `Home facts`
    `the contract is for a relevant interest in land with the home on it, or to be built on it by or for the vendor at the vendor's expense` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the home is to be built by or for the vendor before completion`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person building owns the land, or will own it on completion`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commencement date`                                                    IS A DATE
    `the consideration`                                                        IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value of the home`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the unencumbered value of the land at the commencement date`              IS A NUMBER
    `the commissioner is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme (s 5(4))`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied there is no scheme despite s 5(5)`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme (s 25EA(2))` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the contract replaces a contract made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a substantially similar home` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner is satisfied there is no scheme despite s 25EA(3)`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- Schedule: "consideration, for an eligible transaction, means-- (a) for a contract for the purchase of a home--the
-- consideration for the purchase; (b) for a contract to have a home built--the total consideration payable for the
-- building work; or (c) for the building of a home by an owner builder--the actual costs to the owner of carrying out
-- the work, excluding any allowance for the owner builder's own labour." The figure is stated on that basis.

`the cap (s 5(6) to (9))` MEANS 750000

DECLARE `Why the transaction is not eligible` IS ONE OF
    `the home is not in Queensland`
    `it is not a home (s 6(1))`
    `the contract is not for land with the home on it or to be built by the vendor (s 5(3))`
    `the person building does not own the land, now or on completion (s 5(1)(b), (c))`
    `it commenced before 1 July 2000`
    `it is not a new home, and it commenced on or after 11 October 2012 (s 5(2))`
    `the contract is part of a scheme to circumvent the grant's limits (s 5(4), (5))`
    `the consideration is $750,000 or more (s 5(6))`
    `the home and land together are worth $750,000 or more (s 5(7) to (9))`

DECLARE `Eligibility of the transaction` IS ONE OF
    `a new home eligible transaction (s 5(1))`
    `an eligible transaction for a home other than a new home (s 5(2))`
    `not an eligible transaction` HAS `because` IS A `Why the transaction is not eligible`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a contract` IF
    CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
    WHEN `building a home as an owner builder` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is part of a scheme (s 5(4), (5))` IF
        `it is a contract` `t`
    AND (   `t`'s `the commissioner is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme (s 5(4))`
         OR (    `t`'s `an option or right to the contract was granted before 1 July 2000`
             AND (NOT (`t`'s `the commissioner is satisfied there is no scheme despite s 5(5)`))))

-- s 5(7): for a purchase, "the unencumbered value of the new home or other home" plus "the unencumbered value of the
-- relevant interest in the land ... at the commencement date". (8) and (9): for a building contract or an owner build,
-- "the consideration for the transaction" plus "the unencumbered value of the land ... at the commencement date".
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total tested against the cap (s 5(7) to (9))` `t` MEANS
    CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
    WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN
        `t`'s `the unencumbered value of the home` PLUS `t`'s `the unencumbered value of the land at the commencement date`
    OTHERWISE
        `t`'s `the consideration` PLUS `t`'s `the unencumbered value of the land at the commencement date`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH AN `Eligibility of the transaction`
`the eligibility of the transaction (s 5)` `t` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`t`'s `the home is in Queensland`))
    THEN `not an eligible transaction` `the home is not in Queensland`
    ELSE IF (NOT (`it is a home (s 6(1))` (`t`'s `the home`)))
         THEN `not an eligible transaction` `it is not a home (s 6(1))`
         ELSE IF `the structure fails`
              THEN `not an eligible transaction` `the structural reason`
              ELSE IF `strictly before` (`t`'s `the commencement date`) `1 July 2000`
                   THEN `not an eligible transaction` `it commenced before 1 July 2000`
                   ELSE IF     (NOT (`it is a new home (s 6(2))` (`t`'s `the home`)))
                           AND (NOT (`strictly before` (`t`'s `the commencement date`) `11 October 2012`))
                        THEN `not an eligible transaction` `it is not a new home, and it commenced on or after 11 October 2012 (s 5(2))`
                        ELSE IF `the contract is part of a scheme (s 5(4), (5))` `t`
                             THEN `not an eligible transaction` `the contract is part of a scheme to circumvent the grant's limits (s 5(4), (5))`
                             ELSE IF `t`'s `the consideration` AT LEAST `the cap (s 5(6) to (9))`
                                  THEN `not an eligible transaction` `the consideration is $750,000 or more (s 5(6))`
                                  ELSE IF `the total tested against the cap (s 5(7) to (9))` `t` AT LEAST `the cap (s 5(6) to (9))`
                                       THEN `not an eligible transaction` `the home and land together are worth $750,000 or more (s 5(7) to (9))`
                                       ELSE IF `it is a new home (s 6(2))` (`t`'s `the home`)
                                            THEN `a new home eligible transaction (s 5(1))`
                                            ELSE `an eligible transaction for a home other than a new home (s 5(2))`
    WHERE
        `the structure fails` MEANS
            CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
            WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN
                (NOT (`t`'s `the contract is for a relevant interest in land with the home on it, or to be built on it by or for the vendor at the vendor's expense`))
            OTHERWISE (NOT (`t`'s `the person building owns the land, or will own it on completion`))
        `the structural reason` MEANS
            CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
            WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN `the contract is not for land with the home on it or to be built by the vendor (s 5(3))`
            OTHERWISE `the person building does not own the land, now or on completion (s 5(1)(b), (c))`

GIVEN `e` IS AN `Eligibility of the transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a new home eligible transaction` IF
    CONSIDER `e`
    WHEN `a new home eligible transaction (s 5(1))` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `e` IS AN `Eligibility of the transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an eligible transaction` IF
    CONSIDER `e`
    WHEN `not an eligible transaction` `r` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Schedule, completed; Regulation r 6 -- completion`

-- Schedule: "completed, for an eligible transaction, means-- (a) for a contract for the purchase of a home-- (i) when
-- the purchaser becomes entitled to possession of the home under the contract; and (ii) if the purchaser is to obtain a
-- registered title to the land on which the home is built--the purchaser's title is registered; or (b) for a contract
-- to have a home built--when the building is ready for occupation as a home and any prescribed completion requirements
-- are complied with; or (c) for the building of a home by an owner builder--" the same. Regulation r 6: "the
-- requirement is that a final inspection certificate under the Building Act 1975 has been issued in relation to the
-- building to which the eligible transaction relates."
DECLARE `Completion facts` HAS
    `the purchaser is entitled to possession of the home under the contract`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purchaser is to obtain a registered title to the land`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the purchaser's title is registered`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the building is ready for occupation as a home`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `a final inspection certificate under the Building Act 1975 has been issued` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the kind`       IS A `Kind of transaction`
      `the completion` IS A `Completion facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction has been completed` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN
            `the completion`'s `the purchaser is entitled to possession of the home under the contract`
        AND (   (NOT (`the completion`'s `the purchaser is to obtain a registered title to the land`))
             OR `the completion`'s `the purchaser's title is registered`)
    OTHERWISE
            `the completion`'s `the building is ready for occupation as a home`
        AND `the completion`'s `a final inspection certificate under the Building Act 1975 has been issued`

§§ `s 20, ss 25EA and 25EB -- the amount of the grant; s 91 -- which version governs`

-- s 20(1): "The amount of a first home owner grant is the lesser of the following-- (a) the consideration for the
-- eligible transaction; (b) either-- (i) for a new home eligible transaction--$30,000; or (ii) for another eligible
-- transaction--$7,000." (2): "new home eligible transaction means an eligible transaction mentioned in section 5(1)."
`the s 20 amount for a new home eligible transaction` MEANS 30000
`the s 20 amount for another eligible transaction`    MEANS 7000

GIVEN `new home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the consideration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount under s 20` `new home` `the consideration` MEANS
    IF `new home`
    THEN min `the consideration` `the s 20 amount for a new home eligible transaction`
    ELSE min `the consideration` `the s 20 amount for another eligible transaction`

-- s 25EA(1): a relevant eligible transaction is a s 5(1) eligible transaction that is a purchase contract or a
-- comprehensive home building contract "made between 20 November 2023 and 30 June 2026, both dates inclusive", or an
-- owner build "if the building work starts" between those dates. READING: the start of the building work is taken as
-- the commencement date (schedule: "the date when laying the foundations for the home starts"). s 25EB: "Despite
-- section 20, the amount ... is the lesser of ... (a) the consideration for the transaction; (b) $30,000."
`the s 25EB amount` MEANS 30000

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contract is part of a scheme (s 25EA(2), (3))` IF
        `it is a contract` `t`
    AND (   `t`'s `the commissioner is satisfied the contract is part of a scheme (s 25EA(2))`
         OR (    (   `t`'s `the contract replaces a contract made before 20 November 2023 for the same or a substantially similar home`
                  OR `t`'s `an option or right to the contract was granted before 20 November 2023`)
             AND (NOT (`t`'s `the commissioner is satisfied there is no scheme despite s 25EA(3)`))))

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a relevant eligible transaction (s 25EA)` IF
        `it is a new home eligible transaction` (`the eligibility of the transaction (s 5)` `t`)
    AND `on or before` `20 November 2023` (`t`'s `the commencement date`)
    AND `on or before` (`t`'s `the commencement date`) `30 June 2026`
    AND (NOT (`the contract is part of a scheme (s 25EA(2), (3))` `t`))

-- s 91: for a transaction whose commencement date is before 1 July 2026 the Act applies "as if this Act had not been
-- amended by" the 2026 amending Act, part 3, which is not deposited. Only a relevant eligible transaction (whose amount
-- s 25EB fixes "despite section 20") has an amount the deposit can give; see the module header.
GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deposited text governs the transaction` IF
    `on or before` `20 November 2023` (`t`'s `the commencement date`)

DECLARE `Amount answer` IS ONE OF
    `the grant is` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no grant: not an eligible transaction` HAS `because` IS A `Why the transaction is not eligible`
    `not covered: the amount is set by a version of the Act that is not deposited`

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
GIVETH AN `Amount answer`
`the amount of the grant for` `t` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the deposited text governs the transaction` `t`))
    THEN `not covered: the amount is set by a version of the Act that is not deposited`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the eligibility of the transaction (s 5)` `t`
         WHEN `not an eligible transaction` `r` THEN `no grant: not an eligible transaction` `r`
         OTHERWISE
             IF (NOT (`strictly before` (`t`'s `the commencement date`) `1 July 2026`))
             THEN `the grant is` (`the amount under s 20` (`it is a new home eligible transaction` (`the eligibility of the transaction (s 5)` `t`)) (`t`'s `the consideration`))
             ELSE IF `it is a relevant eligible transaction (s 25EA)` `t`
                  THEN `the grant is` (min (`t`'s `the consideration`) `the s 25EB amount`)
                  ELSE `not covered: the amount is set by a version of the Act that is not deposited`

§§ `ss 10 and 17, Regulation r 3 -- when the grant is payable, and who must apply`

-- s 17: "(1) All interested persons must be applicants. (2) ... an interested person is a person who is, or will be, on
-- completion of the eligible transaction ..., an owner of the relevant home, other than a person prescribed under a
-- regulation." Regulation r 3(1): "(a) if a person is the holder of a relevant interest in land mentioned in section
-- 2(1)--a person who is the holder of another relevant interest in the land; (b) the housing chief executive if, under
-- the scheme ... known as the 'Pathways Shared Equity Loan' scheme-- (i) the housing chief executive holds, or will
-- hold, not more than 40% of the estate in fee simple ...; and (ii) the eligible transaction ... is financed by the
-- housing department; and (iii) the applicant is a tenant of the relevant home."
DECLARE `Other owner facts` HAS
    `will be an owner of the home on completion`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an applicant`                                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant's interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and this person holds another relevant interest in the land` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds or will hold not more than 40% of the fee simple`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the transaction is financed by the housing department`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the applicant is a tenant of the home`                                    IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the owner` IS AN `Other owner facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an interested person (s 17(2), Regulation r 3)` IF
        `the owner`'s `will be an owner of the home on completion`
    AND (NOT (`the owner`'s `the applicant's interest is one declared by Regulation r 2(1), and this person holds another relevant interest in the land`))
    AND (NOT (    `the owner`'s `is the housing chief executive under the Pathways Shared Equity Loan scheme`
              AND `the owner`'s `holds or will hold not more than 40% of the fee simple`
              AND `the owner`'s `the transaction is financed by the housing department`
              AND `the owner`'s `the applicant is a tenant of the home`))

GIVEN `the owner` IS AN `Other owner facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17 is met for the person` IF
    (NOT (`the person is an interested person (s 17(2), Regulation r 3)` `the owner`)) OR `the owner`'s `is an applicant`

-- s 10(1): payable "if-- (a) the applicant or, if there are 2 or more of them, each of the applicants complies with the
-- eligibility criteria; and (b) the transaction ... (i) is an eligible transaction; and (ii) has been completed." (2):
-- exemptions under the Act. (3): "Only 1 first home owner grant is payable for the same eligible transaction." s 19(2):
-- the commissioner may authorise payment before completion. s 22(1): payment "in anticipation of compliance with the
-- residence requirements" if satisfied each applicant intends to comply. s 69A(6): where a disqualifying arrangement
-- exists the commissioner "may" refuse, reverse or recover; that the commissioner has done so is a fact.
-- Criterion 5 looks forward; the answer says the grant is payable subject to it.
DECLARE `Why the grant is not payable` IS ONE OF
    `the transaction is not an eligible transaction` HAS `reason` IS A `Why the transaction is not eligible`
    `an applicant does not meet criteria 1 to 4` HAS `answer` IS A `Criteria answer`
    `another joint applicant does not meet criteria 1 to 4`
    `an interested person is not an applicant (s 17)`
    `a grant has already been paid for this transaction (s 10(3))`
    `the commissioner has refused it for a disqualifying arrangement (s 69A)`

DECLARE `Payable answer` IS ONE OF
    `payable, subject to the residence requirements (s 15), which the commissioner may pay in anticipation of (s 22)`
    `not yet payable: the transaction is not completed, unless the commissioner authorises payment before completion (s 19(2))`
    `not payable` HAS `because` IS A `Why the grant is not payable`
    `not covered: the transaction commenced before 20 November 2023`

DECLARE `Application facts` HAS
    `the transaction`                                                          IS A `Transaction facts`
    `the completion`                                                           IS A `Completion facts`
    `the main applicant`                                                       IS AN `Applicant facts`
    `there is another joint applicant`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other joint applicant meets criteria 1 to 4`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the other owner`                                                          IS AN `Other owner facts`
    `a grant has already been paid for the same transaction`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commissioner has refused or reversed it for a disqualifying arrangement (s 69A)` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN `Application facts`
GIVETH A `Payable answer`
`whether the grant is payable (s 10)` `the application` MEANS
    IF (NOT (`the deposited text governs the transaction` (`the application`'s `the transaction`)))
    THEN `not covered: the transaction commenced before 20 November 2023`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the eligibility of the transaction (s 5)` (`the application`'s `the transaction`)
         WHEN `not an eligible transaction` `r` THEN `not payable` (`the transaction is not an eligible transaction` `r`)
         OTHERWISE
             CONSIDER `the criteria 1 to 4 answer for` (`the application`'s `the main applicant`)
             WHEN `meets criteria 1 to 4` THEN `the rest`
             OTHERWISE `not payable` (`an applicant does not meet criteria 1 to 4` (`the criteria 1 to 4 answer for` (`the application`'s `the main applicant`)))
    WHERE
        `the rest` MEANS
            IF     `the application`'s `there is another joint applicant`
               AND (NOT (`the application`'s `the other joint applicant meets criteria 1 to 4`))
            THEN `not payable` `another joint applicant does not meet criteria 1 to 4`
            ELSE IF (NOT (`s 17 is met for the person` (`the application`'s `the other owner`)))
                 THEN `not payable` `an interested person is not an applicant (s 17)`
                 ELSE IF `the application`'s `a grant has already been paid for the same transaction`
                      THEN `not payable` `a grant has already been paid for this transaction (s 10(3))`
                      ELSE IF `the application`'s `the commissioner has refused or reversed it for a disqualifying arrangement (s 69A)`
                           THEN `not payable` `the commissioner has refused it for a disqualifying arrangement (s 69A)`
                           ELSE IF `the transaction has been completed` (`the application`'s `the transaction`'s `kind`) (`the application`'s `the completion`)
                                THEN `payable, subject to the residence requirements (s 15), which the commissioner may pay in anticipation of (s 22)`
                                ELSE `not yet payable: the transaction is not completed, unless the commissioner authorises payment before completion (s 19(2))`

§§ `s 16 -- the application period`

-- s 16(3): "The application may only be made within a period (the application period)-- (a) starting on the
-- commencement date of the eligible transaction ...; and (b) ending 1 year after the completion of the eligible
-- transaction". (4): "However, the commissioner may allow an application to be made before or after the application
-- period." Schedule: "commencement date ... (a) for a contract ...--the date when the contract is made; or (b) for the
-- building of a home by an owner builder-- (i) the date when laying the foundations for the home starts; or (ii)
-- another date the commissioner considers appropriate".
GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the application period` `the completion date` MEANS `1 year after` `the completion date`

GIVEN `the day of application`   IS A DATE
      `the commencement date`    IS A DATE
      `the completion date`      IS A DATE
      `the commissioner allows it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application may be made on that day (s 16(3), (4))` IF
        (    `on or before` `the commencement date` `the day of application`
         AND `on or before` `the day of application` (`the last day of the application period` `the completion date`))
    OR  `the commissioner allows it`

§§ `s 22(2), s 22A, s 23 -- repaying on the conditions of payment`

-- s 22(2): if paid in anticipation and "the residence requirements are not complied with, the applicants must within 14
-- days after the relevant date-- (a) give written notice of that fact to the commissioner; and (b) repay the amount of
-- the grant." (3): "the relevant date is the earlier of-- (a) the end of the period allowed for compliance with the
-- residence requirements; (b) the date on which it first becomes apparent that the residence requirements will not be
-- complied with during the period allowed for compliance." READING: the period allowed for compliance ends when the
-- required occupation would end if it started on the last day to start. (5): failing the condition "without reasonable
-- excuse" is an offence, "Maximum penalty--40 penalty units". (4): for a joint application each applicant is liable,
-- but compliance by one is compliance by all.
`the days to notify and repay after the relevant date (s 22(2))` MEANS 14

GIVEN `the residence`       IS A `Residence facts`
      `the completion date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the end of the period allowed for compliance` `the residence` `the completion date` MEANS
    `add months to` (`the last day to start occupying the home` `the residence` `the completion date`) (`the months the applicant must occupy the home` `the residence`)

GIVEN `the residence`       IS A `Residence facts`
      `the completion date` IS A DATE
      `the day it first became apparent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the relevant date (s 22(3))` `the residence` `the completion date` `the day it first became apparent` MEANS
    IF `strictly before` `the day it first became apparent` (`the end of the period allowed for compliance` `the residence` `the completion date`)
    THEN `the day it first became apparent`
    ELSE `the end of the period allowed for compliance` `the residence` `the completion date`

GIVEN `the relevant date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify and repay (s 22(2))` `the relevant date` MEANS
    `add days to` `the relevant date` `the days to notify and repay after the relevant date (s 22(2))`

-- s 22A(1): applies if "(a) a first home owner grant is paid before the completion of a relevant transaction; and (b)
-- on completion of the transaction-- (i) the unencumbered value of a new home or other home ... results in the
-- transaction not being an eligible transaction under section 5(7); or (ii) the consideration ... results in the
-- transaction not being an eligible transaction under section 5(8) or (9)." (4): a relevant transaction is a building
-- contract, an owner build, or "a contract mentioned in section 5(3)(b)" (land on which the vendor is to build). (2):
-- "The applicant ... must within 28 days after completion ... (a) give written notice ... that the transaction is not
-- an eligible transaction; and (b) repay the amount of the grant. Maximum penalty--40 penalty units." The values are
-- those found on completion.
`the days to notify and repay after completion (s 22A(2))` MEANS 28

GIVEN `t` IS A `Transaction facts`
      `the grant was paid before completion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22A applies` IF
        `the grant was paid before completion`
    AND `it is a relevant transaction (s 22A(4))`
    AND `the total tested against the cap (s 5(7) to (9))` `t` AT LEAST `the cap (s 5(6) to (9))`
    WHERE
        `it is a relevant transaction (s 22A(4))` MEANS
            CONSIDER `t`'s `kind`
            WHEN `a contract to buy a home` THEN `t`'s `the home is to be built by or for the vendor before completion`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the completion date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to notify and repay (s 22A(2))` `the completion date` MEANS
    `add days to` `the completion date` `the days to notify and repay after completion (s 22A(2))`

-- ss 22(5), 22A(2), 23(4): "Maximum penalty--40 penalty units." The value of a penalty unit is set by the Penalties and
-- Sentences Act 1992 and its regulation, not deposited: an input.
`the maximum penalty in penalty units (ss 22(5), 22A(2), 23(4))` MEANS 40

§§ `Part 4 Division 3 -- repayment, penalty, debt and charge (ss 47 to 49, Regulation r 4)`

-- s 47(1): the commissioner "may, by written notice, require an applicant or former applicant ... to repay an amount
-- paid on the application if the amount was paid in error (the error amount)." (2): if paid "because of a
-- contravention of section 42 or 43" (false or misleading documents or statements), "a penalty of not more than the
-- error amount". (3): if the applicant "fails to make a repayment required under subsection (1) or the conditions of
-- the grant", also "a penalty of not more than the error amount". (5): the notice must give reasons, the 60 days to
-- object, and how. READING: (2) and (3) are separate penalties, each capped at the error amount; where both apply the
-- most is twice it. For a failure to repay under a condition of the grant, the cap is read as the amount to be repaid.
GIVEN `the error amount` IS A NUMBER
      `paid because of a false or misleading document or statement (ss 42, 43)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the repayment required was not made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most penalty the commissioner may impose (s 47(2), (3))` `the error amount` `paid because of a false or misleading document or statement (ss 42, 43)` `the repayment required was not made` MEANS
    (IF `paid because of a false or misleading document or statement (ss 42, 43)` THEN `the error amount` ELSE 0)
    PLUS (IF `the repayment required was not made` THEN `the error amount` ELSE 0)

-- s 48(2): a liability to pay or repay "if the requirement attaches to 2 or more persons, joint and several". (3): it is
-- "a debt payable to the commissioner". (4), (5): an arrangement for payment by instalments "may include provision for
-- the payment of interest".
GIVEN `the number of persons the requirement attaches to` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability is joint and several (s 48(2))` IF `the number of persons the requirement attaches to` AT LEAST 2

-- Regulation r 4(2): interest under an instalment arrangement "is payable at an annual rate equal to the sum of the bank
-- bill yield rate, rounded to the nearest second decimal place, and 8%." (3): the bank bill yield rate is "the monthly
-- average yield of 90-day bank accepted bills published by the Reserve Bank of Australia for the month of May in the
-- financial year immediately before the financial year in which the day occurs." That published rate is not deposited:
-- an input, in per cent a year. READING: a half rounds up.
GIVEN `the bank bill yield rate, per cent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the instalment interest rate, per cent a year (Regulation r 4)` `the bank bill yield rate, per cent` MEANS
    (TRUNC (`the bank bill yield rate, per cent` PLUS 0.005) 2) PLUS 8

-- s 49(1), (2), (2A): if an applicant or former applicant "liable to pay an amount to which section 48 applies has an
-- interest in the land on which the home ... is fixed", the liability "is a first charge on the applicant's interest in
-- the land" with "priority over all other encumbrances". (4): after payment the commissioner "must, as soon as
-- practicable ..., lodge ... a request to release the charge". (6): the registration and release fees are payable by
-- the applicant.
GIVEN `liable to an amount to which s 48 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `has an interest in the land on which the home is fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the liability is a first charge on the interest in the land (s 49)` IF
    `liable to an amount to which s 48 applies` AND `has an interest in the land on which the home is fixed`

§§ `Part 5 -- objections and review (ss 56 to 59)`

-- s 56(1), (1A): an applicant or former applicant "dissatisfied with a decision of the commissioner-- (a) on the
-- applicant's ... application for the grant; or (b) to require payment of an amount under section 47" may lodge a
-- written objection. (2): "The grounds of objection must be stated fully and in detail". (3): "within 60 days after the
-- objector receives notice of the decision." (4): if satisfied of "a reasonable excuse", the commissioner "may extend the
-- time". s 58(1): the commissioner "must give written notice to the objector of the commissioner's decision on the
-- objection." s 59: an objector "dissatisfied with the commissioner's decision on the objection may apply, within 60
-- days after the objector receives notice of the commissioner's decision ..., to QCAT for a review". READING: the day
-- notice is received is left out of the count, so day 60 after it is the last day.
`the days to object (s 56(3))`           MEANS 60
`the days to apply to QCAT (s 59)`       MEANS 60

GIVEN `the day notice of the decision was received` IS A DATE
      `the commissioner has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day of the extended time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object` `the day notice of the decision was received` `the commissioner has extended the time` `the last day of the extended time` MEANS
    IF `the commissioner has extended the time`
    THEN `the last day of the extended time`
    ELSE `add days to` `the day notice of the decision was received` `the days to object (s 56(3))`

GIVEN `the day notice of the objection decision was received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to QCAT` `the day notice of the objection decision was received` MEANS
    `add days to` `the day notice of the objection decision was received` `the days to apply to QCAT (s 59)`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the applicant and the commissioner`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule starts, as its comment says. Each rule is written for one applicant; on a
-- joint application each applicant is liable, and compliance by one is compliance by all (ss 22(4), 22A(3), 23(3)).
DECLARE `FHOG party` IS ONE OF `the applicant`, `the commissioner`

DECLARE `FHOG act` IS ONE OF
    `start to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
    `stop occupying the home as principal place of residence`
    `give the commissioner written notice that the residence requirements are not complied with`
    `give the commissioner written notice that the transaction is not an eligible transaction`
    `give the commissioner notice of non-compliance with the condition`
    `repay the grant` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `repay the amount the notice requires` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `impose a penalty amount` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the penalty amount` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the amount the charge secures`
    `lodge a request to release the charge`
    `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail`
    `give the objector written notice of the decision on the objection`
    `apply to QCAT for a review of the decision on the objection`

-- s 22(2): the 14-day duty. Clock starts on the relevant date.
GIVEN `the grant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
`the s 22(2) duty to notify and repay` `the grant` MEANS
        (PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `give the commissioner written notice that the residence requirements are not complied with`
         WITHIN `the days to notify and repay after the relevant date (s 22(2))`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 22(2)(a), (5): written notice to the commissioner within 14 days after the relevant date (maximum penalty 40 penalty units)")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `repay the grant` (EXACTLY `the grant`)
         WITHIN `the days to notify and repay after the relevant date (s 22(2))`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 22(2)(b), (5): repay the grant within 14 days after the relevant date (maximum penalty 40 penalty units; s 47(3) penalty)")

-- s 15(1): the continuous occupation. The required period runs from the first day of occupation to the day before the
-- day it ends, so moving out on any day up to and including that day breaks it: SHANT stop WITHIN that many days.
-- Clock starts on the first day of occupation.
GIVEN `the days the occupation must last` IS A NUMBER
      `the grant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
`the s 15(1) occupation` `the days the occupation must last` `the grant` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    SHANT `stop occupying the home as principal place of residence`
    WITHIN `the days the occupation must last`
    LEST  `the s 22(2) duty to notify and repay` `the grant`

GIVEN `the residence` IS A `Residence facts`
      `the day occupation started` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days the occupation must last from` `the residence` `the day occupation started` MEANS
    (`the days from` `the day occupation started` `to` (`the day the required period ends` `the residence` `the day occupation started`)) MINUS 1

-- s 15 with s 22: an applicant paid in anticipation (s 22(1)) must start to occupy the home as principal place of
-- residence within the time allowed (s 15(3)) and stay for the required period (s 15(1)); if not, the s 22(2) duty
-- follows. Clock starts on the day of completion. Where the grant has not been paid, criterion 5 is a condition of
-- entitlement only (s 10(1)(a)) and is answered by `the residence answer`, not by this rule.
GIVEN `the days allowed to start`          IS A NUMBER
      `the start deadline applies`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days the occupation must last`  IS A NUMBER
      `exempt from s 15(1)`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant`                          IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
DECIDE `s 15 and s 22(2) -- an applicant paid in anticipation must live in the home, or give notice and repay within 14 days` IS
    IF `exempt from s 15(1)`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE IF `the start deadline applies`
         THEN PARTY `the applicant`
              MUST  `start to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
              WITHIN `the days allowed to start`
              HENCE `the s 15(1) occupation` `the days the occupation must last` `the grant`
              LEST  `the s 22(2) duty to notify and repay` `the grant`
         ELSE PARTY `the applicant`
              MUST  `start to occupy the home as principal place of residence`
              HENCE `the s 15(1) occupation` `the days the occupation must last` `the grant`

-- s 22A(2): notice and repayment within 28 days after completion. Clock starts on the day of completion.
GIVEN `it applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the grant`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
DECIDE `s 22A -- paid early and over the cap on completion, the applicant must give notice and repay within 28 days` IS
    IF `it applies`
    THEN    (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `give the commissioner written notice that the transaction is not an eligible transaction`
             WITHIN `the days to notify and repay after completion (s 22A(2))`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 22A(2)(a): written notice within 28 days after completion (maximum penalty 40 penalty units)")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `repay the grant` (EXACTLY `the grant`)
             WITHIN `the days to notify and repay after completion (s 22A(2))`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 22A(2)(b): repay the grant within 28 days after completion (maximum penalty 40 penalty units)")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 23(1), (2): the commissioner may pay on "reasonable conditions", which may require the applicant "(a) to give
-- notice of non-compliance with the condition within a period stated in the condition; and (b) to repay the grant
-- within a period stated in the condition." (4): failing to comply "without reasonable excuse" is an offence, 40 penalty
-- units. The periods are the condition's: inputs. Clock starts on the day of non-compliance.
GIVEN `the condition has not been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the days the condition allows for notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the days the condition allows to repay`   IS A NUMBER
      `the grant`                                IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
DECIDE `s 23 -- on breaking a condition of the grant, the applicant must give notice and repay within the periods the condition states` IS
    IF `the condition has not been complied with`
    THEN    (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `give the commissioner notice of non-compliance with the condition`
             WITHIN `the days the condition allows for notice`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 23(2)(a), (4): notice of non-compliance within the period the condition states (maximum penalty 40 penalty units)")
        RAND
            (PARTY `the applicant`
             MUST  `repay the grant` (EXACTLY `the grant`)
             WITHIN `the days the condition allows to repay`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 23(2)(b), (4): repay the grant within the period the condition states (maximum penalty 40 penalty units)")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 47(1), (3): the applicant must repay the error amount the notice requires; if not, the commissioner may impose a
-- penalty of not more than the error amount, which is then a debt (s 48(1)(b), (3)). The Act states no period for
-- the repayment: the notice's period is an input. Clock starts on the day the notice is received.
GIVEN `the penalty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
`the duty to pay the penalty amount` `the penalty` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `pay the penalty amount` (EXACTLY `the penalty`)

GIVEN `the error amount`          IS A NUMBER
      `the days the notice allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
DECIDE `s 47 -- the applicant must repay the error amount; if not, the commissioner may impose a penalty of up to that amount` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `repay the amount the notice requires` (EXACTLY `the error amount`)
    WITHIN `the days the notice allows`
    LEST
        PARTY `the commissioner`
        MAY   `impose a penalty amount` `the penalty` PROVIDED `the penalty` AT MOST `the error amount`
        HENCE `the duty to pay the penalty amount` `the penalty`

-- s 49(4): once the amount the charge secures is paid, the commissioner must lodge a request to release the charge, "as
-- soon as practicable" (no fixed period, so no WITHIN). Paying is the applicant's choice: not paying is no breach of
-- this rule (the debt stays, s 48(3)). Clock starts on the day the charge is registered.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
`the commissioner must release the charge` MEANS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `lodge a request to release the charge`

GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
DECIDE `s 49(4) -- once the amount is paid, the commissioner must release the charge` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO    `pay the amount the charge secures`
    HENCE `the commissioner must release the charge`
    LEST  FULFILLED

-- ss 56 to 59: objecting is a choice (DO ... LEST FULFILLED); an objection in time must be decided and notified (s 58,
-- no period stated); then the objector may apply to QCAT within 60 days of receiving that notice (s 59). READING: the
-- day of the commissioner's notice is the day it is received. Clock starts on the day notice of the decision is
-- received; `the days allowed to object` is 60, or the extended time (s 56(4)).
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
`the right to apply to QCAT` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO    `apply to QCAT for a review of the decision on the objection`
    WITHIN `the days to apply to QCAT (s 59)`
    LEST  FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
`the commissioner must decide the objection` MEANS
    PARTY `the commissioner`
    MUST  `give the objector written notice of the decision on the objection`
    HENCE `the right to apply to QCAT`

GIVEN `the days allowed to object` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `FHOG party` `FHOG act`
DECIDE `ss 56 to 59 -- the applicant may object within 60 days, and then apply to QCAT within 60 days of the decision` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO    `lodge a written objection stating the grounds fully and in detail`
    WITHIN `the days allowed to object`
    HENCE `the commissioner must decide the objection`
    LEST  FULFILLED
